Subject: [PATCH] netfs: allow selecting the support core directly

Expose NETFS_SUPPORT so configs/kernel.config can build the netfs and
FS-Cache core into the kernel independently of filesystem consumers.
Keep its existing tristate type and default unchanged.

--- a/fs/netfs/Kconfig
+++ b/fs/netfs/Kconfig
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 
 config NETFS_SUPPORT
-	tristate
+	tristate "Network filesystem support"
 	help
 	  This option enables support for network filesystems, including
 	  helpers for high-level buffered I/O, abstracting out read
